ng AX140 when none is given) and the generated summary as its description (series, x range, minimum, maximum, last value, omissions). It has no tab stop and no pointer-only behavior, so nothing is available to a mouse that is not available to a keyboard. | Accessibility-tree snapshot; a page of 40 has zero added tab stops |\n   207\t| C2 | The fidelity rules still hold: zero baseline for bar and area (F1), gaps (F2), diagnostics (F3), simplified drawing (F5), sorting (F11), no motion (I5), scheme from the page (L4). | The same fixtures as the full charts |\n   208\t| C3 | It fills its container at any size from 24×16 CSS px up; with no definite height it is 32 px tall. | Size tests |\n   209\t| C4 | With more than one series, lines differ by dash as well as color, since there is no legend; AX131 suggests one series per compact chart. | Two-series fixture |\n   210\t| C5 | When values were left out (F12), the description says so and a small marker with a text equivalent appears in the corner. | `dirty` fixture in compact mode |\n   211\t\n   212\tA compact chart does not give access to every value; the summary is its alternative. An author who needs every value reachable uses the full chart.\n   213\t\n106-  readonly slot: Uint8Array;\n107-  /** Index of the caller's row each slot came from, -1 where there is none. null means \"slot i came from row i\" (typed columns). */\n108-  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n109-}\n110-\n111-/** One series of a point frame (scatter): its own x and y, sorted by x then y. */\n112:export interface PointSeries {\n113-  readonly key: string;\n114-  readonly label: string;\n115-  readonly drawable: boolean;\n116-  readonly x: Float64Array;\n117-  readonly y: Float64Array;\n118-  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n--\n121-   * plotted (the rows AX103 and AX106 report). Sorted by x, duplicates kept. They are not points: nothing is\n122-   * drawn or picked for them. They exist so the table can list them as \"No data\" (spec F2 and F12: the note\n123-   * sends the reader to the table, so the table must show every row that was left out). Absent or empty when\n124-   * there are none. With `missing: 'zero'` on the y field, null and absent values are points with y = 0 instead\n125-   * and do not appear here; a value that cannot be plotted is never imputed.\n126-   */\n127:  readonly missingX?: Float64Array;\n128:  /** Source row index of each entry of `missingX`, in the same order; present whenever `missingX` and `row` are. */\n129:  readonly missingRow?: Int32Array;\n130-}\n131-\n132-/**\n133- * The normalized, lossless data. Immutable: an update or append produces a new frame with a higher revision.\n134- * Buffers may be shared between revisions; a streaming store appends into spare capacity and hands out\n135- * subarray views, so an append does not copy what is already there.\n--\n148-  /** Number of x slots. */\n149-  readonly length: number;\n150-  readonly xLabel: string;\n151-  readonly yLabel: string | null;\n152-}\n153-\n154:export interface PointFrame extends FrameBase {\n155-  readonly shape: 'points';\n156-  readonly xKind: Exclude<XKind, 'category'>;\n157-  readonly timeZone: string | null;\n158:  readonly series: readonly PointSeries[];\n159-  readonly xLabel: string;\n160-  readonly yLabel: string;\n161-  readonly xUnit: string | null;\n162-  readonly yUnit: string | null;\n163-}\n164-\n--\n172-  readonly row: Int32Array | null;\n173-  readonly valueLabel: string;\n174-  readonly unit: string | null;\n175-  readonly valueScale: 'percent' | 'ratio' | null;\n176-}\n177-\n178:export type Frame = AlignedFrame | PointFrame | DonutFrame;\n179-\n180-/**\n181- * Join rule for lines and areas (spec F2). Two consecutive SLOT_VALUE slots i < j of one series are joined\n182- * if and only if every slot strictly between them is SLOT_NO_ROW. A value with no joined neighbour on either\n183- * side is an isolated point and must be drawn as a visible point.\n184- */\n--\n299-  readonly drawSlots: read