ld, position);\n   206\t    }\n   207\t  }\n   208\t}\n   209\t\n   210\t/**\n   211\t * The x positions of the first frame's slots, for history that outlives the store's first buffer. A view on the\n   212\t * caller's own column costs nothing and, unlike a view on the store's buffer, never pins a superseded copy.\n   213\t */\n   214\tfunction prefixPositions(table: Table, field: string, x: XData, buffers: FrameBuffers): Float64Array {\n   215\t  return table.columns?.[field] === x.positions && x.positions.length === buffers.end ? x.positions : buffers.x.subarray(0, buffers.end);\n   216\t}\n   217\t\n   218\tfunction cadences(options: Fields, table: Table, x: XData, axis: XColumn, buffers: FrameBuffers) {\n   219\t  if (table.columns && options.series === null && x.order === null && x.positions.length > 0 && buffers.end === x.positions.length) {\n   220\t    // Each wide series observes the same sorted x column. Keep appended history\n   221\t    // separate so it cannot overwrite the prefix of a competing frame.\n   222\t    const prefix = prefixPositions(table, options.x.field, x, buffers);\n   223\t    const window = new Observations(prefix);\n   224\t    const initial = readCadence(axis, window);\n   225\t    return {\n   226\t      history: new Map(options.values.map(field => [field.field, { ...initial }])),\n   227\t      observations: new Map(options.values.map(field => [field.field, window.fork()])),\n   228\t      duplicates: new Map<string, StoreMap<number, true>>(),\n   229\t    };\n   230\t  }\n   231\t  const keys = seriesKeys(table, options.series);\n   232\t  const observations = new Map<string, Observations>();\n   233\t  const duplicates = new Map<string, StoreMap<number, true>>();\n   234\t  const last = new Map<string, number>();\n   235\t  eachObservation(options, x, keys, (key, position) => {\n   236\t    let window = observations.get(key);\n   237\t    if (!window) observations.set(key, window = new Observations());\n   238\t    if (position