{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/interaction-final.fix.report.md | rg -n -i 'corridor|readout|evict|formatter|test' -C 2; git show bbd7564:packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-hold.browser.test.ts | nl -ba | sed -n '144,243p'; git show bbd7564:packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts | rg -n 'function (commit|attach|release|detach)|\\\\bcommit\\\\(state|readoutMode|expire.*[hH]old|recheck|validateHold|hold =|holding =|corridor'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"git show bbd7564:reviews/2026-11-18/impl/wp/interaction-final.fix.report.md | rg -n -i 'corridor|readout|evict|formatter|test' -C 2; git show bbd7564:packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-hold.browser.test.ts | nl -ba | sed -n '144,243p'; git show bbd7564:packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts | rg -n 'function (commit|attach|release|detach)|\\\\bcommit\\\\(state|readoutMode|expire.*[hH]old|recheck|validateHold|hold =|holding =|corridor'\"","aggregated_output":"5-**Controller (`src/core/chart.ts` `measure()`, around line 184).** It still treats any plot scale within 2% of 1 as 1. Under `scale(1.015)` on an ancestor, the layout then believes the plot is 1.5% wider than it is, so the marks overflow and are clipped. Picking stays correct in my layer, because I map against the marks as drawn. The fix is to divide by the computed size: `width = rect.width / k`, with `k = rect.width / parseFloat(getComputedStyle(plot).width)`, and the same for height. Treat `|k − 1| < 1e-5` as 1. That tolerance is only the rounding of the computed value to six significant digits (\"341.531px\" for 341.53125); it is not a transform. Without it, a point drawn exactly on the plot's top edge is picked as outside. That is what emptied T-tooltip-scatter in an intermediate build (`src/dom/mapping.ts` has the same snap).\n6-\n7:**Controller, finding 12.** I added `readoutMode?: 'floating' | 'strip' | 'none'` to `ControlsState`. `readoutOf()` in `dom/interaction.ts` is the only place it is read: it uses `readoutMode`, else the old `readout` boolean. 'none' means no floating tooltip, no strip and no pin; the datum is still highlighted. The controller's cast can now be dropped.\n8-\n9-**Public messages (`public.ts`, fixed), C2-8.** Arbitrary drag ranges still have no non-dragging equivalent (WCAG 2.5.7). The smallest answer is two clicks, and that needs a labelled control. The change: add one `Messages` key, for example `selectRange: 'Select range'`, for a toolbar toggle; while it is on, the next two plot clicks set the range's two ends through the same `requestZoom` path. I did not add it because it changes the public interface.\n--\n18-|---|---|\n19-| `npm run typecheck` | clean |\n20:| `npx vitest run packages/axylo/test/core` | Test Files 13 passed, Tests 207 passed |\n21:| chart + a11y, SVG | Test Files 17 passed, Tests 235 passed |\n22:| chart + a11y, canvas | Tests 1 failed, 234 passed (235) |\n23:| acceptance, SVG | Test Files 13 passed, **Tests 555 passed (555)** |\n24-\n25:- **The canvas failure** was the P7 memory test in `lifecycle.browser.test.ts`: non-code heap grew 98,556 B against a 65,536 B limit. It passed in the earlier full canvas run and in two reruns of that test alone, and it also passes on the old bundle. I take it as noise under load from the other agents, not a leak.\n26-- **An earlier acceptance run had one failure** (A1 compact: `window.Axylo` undefined): another agent rebuilt `dist` (deleted and rewritten) during that run. The file passed 46/46 on its own, and the full rerun above was 555/555.\n27-\n--\n32-  - pinned: nothing changes.\n33-  - hover: becomes held when the pointer rested 250 ms within 2 viewport px on the same datum and that datum's content is on show.\n34:  - held: stays while the pointer is inside the hull of the resting point and the content's rectangle (`placement.insideCorridor`). Otherwise it picks afresh on that same move.\n35-  - A pointer that has not rested is never held. There are no per-kind holds left; the scatter/donut rectangle hold is gone.\n36-- **`commit` reconciles before presenting:**\n--\n43-- **Dismissal** is remembered by datum: the x, the slice, or the group's first point; a group that gains coincident points still matches it.\n44-- **Focus** is established in `commit` (the first datum when the proxy is focused and focus is null). State text clears the text cache. Whether the text is rewritten is decided by `datumReading` (identity, values and templates), not by subtracting the position sentence.\n45:- **Placement** is pure (`dom/placement.ts`). Validity is checked against the visible plot (plot ∩ viewport ∩ each clipping ancestor's padding box less scrollbar, per axis), every control and every keyboard ring, with a shift along the free axis. The hole is tested on all four corners against r0 − 5, and only ring strokes count there. The last resort never covers a control or a ring; if nothing works, nothing floats. The tooltip's maximum size is the visible plot.\n46-- **Mapping:** one function (`dom/mapping.ts`), fractional sizes; the limit for rotated, skewed and mirrored ancestors is documented in its comment.\n47-\n48-## The 16 findings\n49-\n50:\"Old\" means the test was run against a bundle built from the pre-pass source (HEAD), through `AXYLO_BUNDLE`. Test files are in `packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/` and `packages/axylo/test/core/`.\n51-\n52:| # | Fixed | Test | Fails on old |\n53-|---|---|---|---|\n54-| 1 | yes | final-hold, finding 1 (Q3 to Q4, then click gives Q4's exact row; scatter B under A's tooltip; donut hole selects nothing) | yes, all 3 |\n55-| 2 | yes | final-pin, finding 2 (active element, value text, ring, tooltip and Enter checked together) | yes |\n56-| 3 | yes: the slice list has roving keys while the plot is not ready (one tab stop) | final-pin, finding 3 | yes |\n57:| 4 | yes | focus-placement (reviewer's arithmetic table, fallback, property test); final-pin clipped card with hit-tests | Node tests: the old function was DOM-bound, so I could not run it; the reviewer's recorded outputs are the counterexamples. The card test passes on old. |\n58-| 5 | yes | final-hold, finding 5 (dense edge line, horizontal bar to strip, isolated scatter point to strip, no-rest converse) | yes, the first 3 |\n59-| 6 | yes: pinned content exposed to the AX tree; pinned \"+N more\" is a button that pages through the rows; the strip keeps at least