{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_83","type":"agent_message","text":"Reviewed commit `bbd7564` using its Git blobs. The Node suite finished with `Test Files 66 passed (66)` and `Tests 1409 passed | 1 skipped (1410)`. The skipped test was the deliberate P7 memory failure. Browser and packed-distribution findings below are source-traced. I treated an append accepted before Pause as eligible for its pending draw.\n\n| Finding | Severity | Status | Evidence at `bbd7564` | Reverting test and basis |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 · Publication and row ownership | Blocker | **Fixed with a new defect** | In-flight rows survive eviction, frame notifications drain after publication, and a superseded frame cannot publish AX199. Formatter re-entry still breaks publication in other ways. [controller.ts:1054](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1054), [controller.ts:1478](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1478) | [“a stage failing after a callback changed the chart…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:72) covers stale AX199 with DX5 expectations. **None** catches removal of the in-flight pin. |\n| 2 · Paused retention | Blocker | **Partly fixed** | Both original sequences are bounded. An unmeasured redraw still resets the retention baseline every time. [controller.ts:1495](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1495), [controller.ts:1504](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1504) | [“paused before the frame of an append…” and “paused with 2 on screen…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:103). Row expectations come from the fixture. The 12-row cap comes from the implementation’s retention policy. |\n| 3 · Failed Resume resurrects old rows | Blocker | **Fixed** | A successful running append supersedes the held revision before accepting the new frame. [controller.ts:728](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:728) | [“display 2, pause, append 3, Resume fails, append 4…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:132). DX5 and fixture-derived row `4`. |\n| 4 · First-append memory and caller-column lifetime | Blocker | **Partly fixed** | Opening still copies contiguous x and y. Implicit rows and smaller spare buffers reduce the cost. The caller-column retention fixes are present. [store-buffers.ts:55](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:55), [controller.ts:681](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:681), [controller.ts:1045](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1045) | [“keeps typed-column rows implicit…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:115), [“after a replacement the first columns are let go…” and “a stream with keep 2…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:483). Contract-derived indexes and independent GC checks. The excluded budget test measured 17,069,760 B against 16,000,000 B. |\n| 5 · DX7 packed download limits | Blocker | **Not fixed** | The 80 and 96 KiB thresholds exist. CI still runs the reporting command without `--check`. The recorded overages are from `a518cbb`. [size.mjs:60](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/scripts/size.mjs:60), [ci.yml:45](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/.github/workflows/ci.yml:45), [STATUS.md:44](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/STATUS.md:44) | **None** for the packed limits. [“size target comparison”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/tests/dist/size.test.ts:11) checks arithmetic. |\n| 6 · Paused validation and re-encoding | Major | **Partly fixed** | `missingRow` preserves the original null-y scatter case, held arrivals are installed before handlers run, and Resume can clear AX101. Re-encoding initializes held view findings to `[]`, and the displayed table still reconstructs rows from plotted slots. [controller.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:605), [controller.ts:642](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:642), [controller.ts:740](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:740), [controller.ts:874](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:874) | [“a ninth series held while paused…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:366), [“scatter, paused…” / “a Resume from an AX103 handler…” / “a missing-field AX101 goes…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:510). Spec and fixture-based. **None** checks that AX130 survives re-encoding. |\n| 7 · Exceptional validation and strict | Major | **Partly fixed** | The titled create case retains AX150 before AX199, and the straightforward strict update rejects. Append has no preparation context, and untitled create still differs from `validate()` by AX140. [controller.ts:530](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:530), [controller.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:662), [stages.ts:171](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/stages.ts:171) | [“an unknown option and a throwing x getter…” and “strict: create with them throws…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:339). Explicit §3.5 codes and last-good-display expectations. Four Cartesian kinds in the parity test. |\n| 8 · Bounded scatter picking and hover payload | Major | **Partly fixed** | The lattice caps counted candidate visits and unused hover payloads are skipped. The first fallback builds an index on the pointer path, and the payload can scan every row sharing x. [scatter-grid.ts:325](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:325), [controller.ts:1600](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1600), [controller.ts:1650](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1650) | [“agrees with a brute-force pick under the device-pixel lattice rule” and the ring cases](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:488). Contract-derived oracle and candidate bound. **None** checks first-pick construction cost or same-x payload work. |\n| 9 · Short-plot readout | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | The controller and DOM support the three modes required by amended I1. The initial strip estimate uses the axis font and can cause a false L8 fallback. [controller.ts:1313](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1313), [interaction.ts:149](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:149), [css.ts:190](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:190) | [“a 330 × 205 container…” and “a plot under 140 px…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:255). I1/L8 thresholds. The Node host does not deduct the real strip height. |\n| 10 · Evicted tooltip corridor | Major | **Fixed** | Category holds remap by exact identity. Commit repicks when the target, anchor, presentation or content rectangle ceases to match. [interaction.ts:1648](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1648), [interaction.ts:1729](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1729), [interaction.ts:1768](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:1768) | [“a stream commit that moves the bands…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/browser/chart/final-hold.browser.test.ts:187) derives the expected band from the fixture and rule 3b. **None** exercises eviction of the held datum itself. |\n| 11 · Cached AX160 and reader note | Major | **Fixed** | Tick failures are cached with the axis parts and republished when the ready layout returns. [axes.ts:85](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:85), [controller.ts:1250](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1250) | [“a throwing y tick formatter: AX160 and the note survive…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:156). §3.5 and F12. |\n| 12 · Mutable dates and zoom round-trip | Major | **Fixed** | Options and zoom snapshot `Date` inputs. Fractional positions are emitted as numbers. [options.ts:44](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/options.ts:44), [controller.ts:195](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:195), [controller.ts:817](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:817) | [“a Date in x.domain mutated and resubmitted…”, “a Date passed to zoom()…”, and “a window between milliseconds…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:175). Fixture timestamps and the public round-trip contract. |\n| 13 · Compact zoom and secondary tick formats | Major | **Fixed** | Compact zoom exits before accepting a window. The resolver reports AX150 for every unused compact tick formatter. [controller.ts:807](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:807), [data/options.ts:239](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/options.ts:239) | [“no event, AX150, and nothing applied when compact is turned off”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:216) and [“compact %s: x and every y field”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/diagnostics/registry.test.ts:266). §3.7 and F3. |\n| 14 · Watcher cleanup and reattachment | Major | **Partly fixed** | Theme setup rolls back and successful reattachment clears font measurements. A failure during reattachment can still leave prior subscriptions live and `watching` set. [watch.ts:34](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/watch.ts:34), [chart.ts:91](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:91), [chart.ts:148](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:148) | [“the theme observer’s observe() throws…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:235) catches a full revert under DX5. Its shared `Set` counts the same callback once across three targets. **None** checks font widths after reattachment or rollback of the full watcher sequence. |\n| 15 · Automatic numeric x endpoints | Major | **Partly fixed** | The original line domain is correct under amended F7. Ordinary scatter uses endpoint tick candidates, but the candidate extent excludes missing-y positions and the layout can drop an endpoint. [spec F7](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/docs/02-product-spec.md:100), [view/index.ts:220](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:220), [axes.ts:137](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:137) | [“a line on x 1.1 to 8.9…” and “a scatter on x 1.1 to 8.9…”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:283). F7 and fixture-derived. Removing the scatter filter in memory failed the scatter test. |\n| 16 · Repeated series cues | Major | **Fixed with a new defect** | Compact bars now have 32 colour/pattern combinations. Scatter’s 64 combinations satisfy amended F9. The compact bar change also makes some previously distinct patterns identical. [scene/bars.ts:11](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:11), [view/index.ts:73](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/view/index.ts:73) | [“spec F9: at least 32 distinct combinations…” → “bar (compact: true)”](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/scene/scene.test.ts:702). F9-derived count. **None** checks the lost non-colour distinction. |\n\n## New defects\n\n1. **Blocker · A typed append can return the wrong source row.** Start a line with typed x `[0,1]`, y `[0,10]`, and `missing: 'zero'`. Append `[{x:2,y:20},{x:3,y:null},{x:4,y:40}]`. Hovering x=2 reports index 0 and `{x:0,y:0}`. When the null forces an explicit index, initialize the identity entries through the slots already written in that batch. [store-buffers.ts:109](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:109), [store.ts:824](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store.ts:824)\n\n2. **Blocker · A hidden, paused chart still retains unbounded history.** Draw x=2 with `keep:1`, Pause, hide the container, then append x=3 through 503 with `keep:1` and let each frame run. The store retains **502 rows**. Normalize the absent displayed frame to `null` before comparing it with the next frame, and keep the baseline stable while unmeasured. [controller.ts:1495](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1495), [controller.ts:1504](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1504)\n\n3. **Blocker · Tick formatter re-entry can starve publication.** Install a tick formatter that calls `update({title:'New title'})` each time. The old title was still visible after six frames, with another frame pending. Key prepared ticks on axis inputs so a title-only update can reuse them. A formatter that instead switches to an unformatted field and throws also delivers a stale AX160 under the new title. Check the frame generation before publishing those findings. [axes.ts:87](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:87), [controller.ts:1250](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1250)\n\n4. **Major · Paused re-encoding loses held findings and raw row information.** Hold a ninth series, change y to another populated field, then call `update({strict:true})`. AX130 disappears and strict succeeds until Resume. In scatter, a displayed row with old `x:null` and valid alternate `u` appears only after Resume when switching x to `u`. Re-encoding a typed `NaN` while paused can also raise a false omission note. Validate both views before accepting either and re-encode the displayed raw window with its typed-column provenance. [controller.ts:605](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:605), [controller.ts:642](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:642), [controller.ts:740](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:740)\n\n5. **Major · A frozen scatter frame changes month precision.** Queue a March `YYYY-MM` point with `keep:1`, Pause before its frame, then append April through December with `keep:1` before drawing. March reads **“Mar 1, 2026”** even though hover still returns the original `{x:'2026-03',y:3}`. Read date precision through the same owned-row accessor as hover. [controller.ts:311](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:311), [controller.ts:1834](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1834)\n\n6. **Major · A throwing getter bypasses strict and can undo teardown.** On a valid strict line, append a row whose x getter throws. The call returns and the chart shows AX199. A nested `update` from a getter also clears the outer strict context. A getter that calls `destroy()` and returns lets the outer update repopulate the destroyed handle’s diagnostics. Keep preparation state local to each call, use it for append, and check liveness before acceptance. [controller.ts:495](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:495), [controller.ts:530](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:530), [controller.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:662)\n\n7. **Major · Scatter still does data-sized work on a pointer move.** The first hover at the centre of a 32,000-point ring builds the lattice even though the counter reports only 2,679 visits. With 50,000 points sharing x and a hover subscriber, picking row 49,999 read **50,001 row indexes** during payload construction. Build the fallback with the lookup and reuse the point index already located by the pick. [scatter-grid.ts:325](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter-grid.ts:325), [scatter.ts:30](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/lookup/scatter.ts:30), [controller.ts:1603](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1603)\n\n8. **Major · Lattice tooltip paging can repeat page one.** Pin the centre pick of that ring at DPR 1. The lookup counts 14 points and provides eight. The pager reconstructs only those eight from raw anchors, so `+6 more` returns the same rows. Page from the winning grid group using the same membership rule that produced the count. [focus.ts:171](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/focus.ts:171), [interaction.ts:662](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/dom/interaction.ts:662)\n\n9. **Major · An estimated strip can blank a readable chart.** Give a donut 112 px of plot room. With the recording host using the CSS strip’s 48 px minimum, the controller estimates 30 px, reserves the strip, then shows AX142 and no marks at 64 px. Use the strip’s own line height or retry without the strip before entering L8. [controller.ts:1315](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1315), [controller.ts:1353](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1353), [css.ts:190](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/theme/css.ts:190)\n\n10. **Major · Narrow scatter still drops the automatic x endpoint.** Draw x `1.1, 8.9, 10.7` with the last y null, then resize the recording host to 185 × 400. The plot remains readable with x domain `[0,12]` and ticks `[0,5,10]`. Use the same extent for domain and tick selection, and apply the coarser-domain fitting path to scatter x. [axes.ts:137](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/axes.ts:137), [layout/index.ts:251](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/layout/index.ts:251)\n\n11. **Major · Watcher acquisition can get stuck on reattachment.** Detach and reattach a chart, with the environment watcher throwing once after the theme watcher starts. The observer path leaves `watching` set and subsequent resize notifications skip setup. Roll back that invocation’s subscriptions and reset `watching` on failure. This is source-traced. [chart.ts:101](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:101), [chart.ts:148](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/chart.ts:148)\n\n12. **Major · Memory accounting omits live buffers.** Draw 1,001 streamed line rows, Pause, then append with `keep:2`. The benchmark reported 8,714 B while the displayed frame alone still held 23,625 B in omitted column buffers. At store level, preparing a competing tail fill and then reading the old frame also creates a cached copy that `ownedBytes()` skips. Count buffers from every live frame with one deduplication set, including already-materialized getter copies. [instrument.ts:149](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/instrument.ts:149), [store-bytes.ts:58](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-bytes.ts:58), [store-buffers.ts:269](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-buffers.ts:269)\n\n13. **Major · Compact bar patterns lose an A5 distinction.** Draw three equal-height series in one compact category. Series indexes 1 and 2 now both use diagonal fill and differ only in colour. Preserve a distinguishable non-colour cue across the palette while keeping the 32 F9 combinations. Adding pattern types would require extending `RectMark.pattern` and both renderers. [scene/bars.ts:18](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/scene/bars.ts:18), [contracts.ts:469](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/contracts.ts:469)\n\n14. **Minor · Scatter retains a duplicate x column after the last missing point is evicted.** Append a null-y row and a valid row, then append another valid row with `keep:2`. `missingX` is gone but `ownedBytes()` still lists `x positions`. Drop that column when every retained row is again represented by the point x column. [store-unaligned.ts:157](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:157), [store-unaligned.ts:187](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/data/store-unaligned.ts:187)\n\n## Claims not confirmed\n\n- The test named “the frame draws 3” actually leaves `[0,1,2]` on screen for that frame, then draws `[4]`. Removing the in-flight pin in memory left all 37 final-review tests green. A focused commit-time eviction probe changed from the correct row to `row:null` with that removal. I also observed a throwing value formatter run again after the first figure write in the Node host. [final-review.test.ts:25](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:25), [controller.ts:1188](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/src/core/controller.ts:1188)\n- The wider snapshot properties compare frame contents and captions. They do not independently check the zoomed marks, skip collapsed and faulted frames, and never exercise scatter hover provenance. The path assertion is an upper bound, and the retention assertion allows eleven extra rows. [final-review.test.ts:442](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:442), [final-review.test.ts:639](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/core/final-review.test.ts:639)\n- The shared-tree reports do not establish browser results, I1/P4 latency, lifetime heap behaviour or packed byte counts for `bbd7564`. The candidate and byte-count tests cover narrower measurements. [scatter.test.ts:516](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/lookup/scatter.test.ts:516), [streaming-storage.test.ts:133](/home/canarit/projects/axylo/packages/axylo/test/data/streaming-storage.test.ts:133)\n\n**This part is not ready for the release acceptance run.** The blockers are the DX7 packed-size gate, defects 1–13 above, and missing focused regressions for in-flight ownership, held-datum eviction and reattachment cleanup and font measurement. The deliberate P7 failure and the redundant scatter x column are outside that blocker list."}}
